{"id":"m68727:problem:fs-idp165246960","rulings":["heat"],"maxOps":6,"en":"During a recent winter month in Sheboygan, Wisconsin, it was necessary to obtain 3500 kWh of heat provided by a natural gas furnace with 89% efficiency to keep a small house warm (the efficiency of a gas furnace is the percent of the heat produced by combustion that is transferred into the house).","is":"Í nýlegum vetrarmánuði í Sheboygan, Wisconsin, var nauðsynlegt að fá 3500 kWst af hita frá jarðgasofni með 89% nýtni til að halda litlu húsi volgu (nýtni gasofns er hlutfall hitans sem myndast við bruna sem flyst inn í húsið)."},
{"id":"m68727:problem:fs-idp165247664","rulings":["heat","temperature"],"maxOps":9,"en":"(a) Assume that natural gas is pure methane and determine the volume of natural gas in cubic feet that was required to heat the house. The average temperature of the natural gas was 56 °F; at this temperature and a pressure of 1 atm, natural gas has a density of 0.681 g/L.","is":"(a) Gerðu ráð fyrir að jarðgas sé hreint metan og ákvarðaðu rúmmál jarðgass í rúmfetum sem þurfti til að hita húsið. Meðalhiti jarðgassins var 56 °F; við þetta hitastig og þrýstinginn 1 atm hefur jarðgas eðlismassann 0,681 g/L."},
